{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971790-correspondence","id":971790,"title":"Correspondence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T23:33:46-07:00","id":971790,"title":"Correspondence","content":"I've searched the book for something to determine the radius/range or a chart for correspondence 1's immediate spatial perceptions rote but couldn't find any.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Correspondence Sphere Ranges<br /> Successes Range Connection<br /> One Line of sight Body sample<br /> Two Very familiar Close possession or companion<br /> Three Familiar Possession or casual friend<br /> Four Visited once Casual acquaintance or object used once<br /> Five Described location Briefly touched or met object or person<br /> Six+ Anywhere on Earth No connection </div> </div> </div>Any ideas or hints how it works or if there's a chart that I've missed in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:17:21-07:00","id":971803,"title":"","content":"I've always treated it as by default having line-of-sight range, in all directions. Think of it as a magickal echolocation. It ends at Intervening non-space. (And sanely doesn't reach into space :P Easily explainable by the metaphysical location of the first horizon.)<br /> That also means, yes, thick fog or smoke can block it. Those would block normal line of sight as well. <i>*technically* glass should block it as well,</i> but that is really also an ST call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:34:25-07:00","id":971805,"title":"","content":"In M20 or &quot;How do you Do that?&quot; I don't really remember which one but anyhow. It says when a mage uses invisibility rote on himself light is bent around him and doesn't reach his eyes which makes him blind and having the +2 penalty but those with corres 1 don't suffer from it and can see normally even with the invisibility on so idk, is that another rote in corres 1 smth, what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:21:12-07:00","id":971824,"title":"","content":"I interpret &quot;Line of Sight&quot; as being figurative. Otherwise, a character with the &quot;Blind&quot; Flaw would gain no new information.<br /> <br /> So I disagree with the idea that obstructions to line of sight would block Corr 1. It's more an indication of a relative area immediately surrounding the user in all directions, and the contours of everything contained therein. I have no set numbers for how large that area would be, but there you go. It's however large the Storyteller wants (and when they think you need to pull out Corr 2). In this model, fog and mist don't do anything to hinder the Mage, nor does darkness. Hence why it's just a boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T02:25:45-07:00","id":971846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971790-correspondence?p=971824#post971824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I interpret &quot;Line of Sight&quot; as being figurative. Otherwise, a character with the &quot;Blind&quot; Flaw would gain no new information.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my case it wasn't related to the eyes or their functionality <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Line-of-sight simply meant all space surrounding the mage in all directions, with them at the center, ending at obstructions in all directions. So our ideas are actually very similiar, except I don't see Corr 1 going behind objects. I actually remember a RAW that hinted at thatalong those lines...<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Nah, can't find it. Nevermind! It's really up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-18-2016, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T02:36:01-07:00","id":971847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/971790-correspondence?p=971805#post971805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In M20 or &quot;How do you Do that?&quot; I don't really remember which one but anyhow. It says when a mage uses invisibility rote on himself light is bent around him and doesn't reach his eyes which makes him blind and having the +2 penalty but those with corres 1 don't suffer from it and can see normally even with the invisibility on so idk, is that another rote in corres 1 smth, what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's just one of the functions in Correspondence Sphere.<br /> <br /> As Ambrosia said, imagine it like echolocation. Line of sight = the surrounding area that you can percieve, with you being in a center of it. Obviously you shouldn't go out with your way like &quot;I can see space aka sky from Earth so I can teleport there with 1 success&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}